{% comment %}
Every step of the goal, each with its MENU — the actions the decider said it may use — and each
menu action's properties as the catalogue declares them. One request per GOAL, not per step: the
steps refer to one another (`%!data%` is the action before it), and a model shown one step in
isolation cannot see that.

The menu is walked off the module catalogue and filtered by what the decider chose, so every
property row comes from the action's own declaration — nothing here restates it.
{% endcomment %}
{{ goal.Name }}
{% for s in goal.Step %}
step {{ s.Index }}: {{ s.Text }}
{%- if s.Body.size > 0 %}
   (its body is step{% if s.Body.size > 1 %}s{% endif %} {% for b in s.Body %}{{ b.Index }}{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}{% endfor %}, indented below — the builder places it; give this step no child)
{%- endif %}
   menu:
{%- for m in modules -%}
{%- for a in m.Action -%}
{%- assign choice = m.Name | append: "." | append: a.Name -%}
{%- if menu[s.Index] contains choice %}
     {{ choice }}
{%- for p in a.Property %}
        {{ p.Name }} ({{ p.Type.Name }}{% if p.Type.Kind %}<{{ p.Type.Kind.Name }}>{% endif %}{% if p.Type.Values %}: one of {{ p.Type.Values | join: ", " }}{% endif %}{% if p.Required %}, required{% else %}, optional{% endif %}{% if p.HasDefault %}, default {{ p.Default }}{% endif %})
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if a.Notes %}
        notes:
{%- assign noteLines = a.Notes | strip | split: "\n" -%}
{%- for line in noteLines %}
          {{ line }}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor %}
{% endfor %}
